  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 21,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.104,
            0.591,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SUMMARY"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.16,
            0.829,
            0.199
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figures that have the same shape and size are said to be "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "congruent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". These figures can be superimposed so that one fits exactly over the other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.199,
            0.829,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While verifying congruence, a figure can be rotated or flipped to make it fit exactly over the other figure via superimposition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.237,
            0.829,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two triangles have the same sidelengths, we say that the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SSS (Side Side Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition is satisfied. The SSS condition guarantees congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.294,
            0.83,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two sides and the included angle of one triangle are equal to the two sides and the included angle of another triangle, we say that the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SAS (Side Angle Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition is satisfied. The SAS condition also guarantees congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.371,
            0.83,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two angles and the included side of one triangle are equal to the two angles and the included angle of another triangle, we say that the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ASA (Angle Side Angle)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition is satisfied. The ASA condition guarantees congruence. Congruence holds even if the side is not included between the angles "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "AAS (Angle Angle Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.466,
            0.829,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a right-angled triangle, the side opposite to the right angle is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "hypotenuse",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.504,
            0.83,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a side and a hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle are equal to a side and the hypotenuse of another right-angled triangle, we say that the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "RHS (Right Hypotenuse Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition is satisfied. The RHS condition also guarantees congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.581,
            0.829,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two triangles need not be congruent if two sides and a non-included angle are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.619,
            0.671,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• In a triangle, angles opposite to equal sides are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.639,
            0.618,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The angles in an equilateral triangle are all 60°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "22"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
